# Node.js servers

- Use Node 22 or newer (`engines.node` is `>=22`).
- Read env once at startup. The BFF exits if `VENDOR_API_KEY` or `VENDOR_API_URL` is missing.
- Do not log `process.env`. What else must stay out of logs is in the security rule.
- Time out each vendor call with `VENDOR_TIMEOUT_MS`. See the performance rule.
- On an unhandled error, log the error and `process.exit(1)`.

```ts
// Bad
console.log(process.env);

// Good
if (!process.env.VENDOR_API_KEY || !process.env.VENDOR_API_URL) {
  console.error("Missing VENDOR_API_KEY or VENDOR_API_URL");
  process.exit(1);
}
```
